  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{s}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{s(t+h)-s(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{\u2032}(6) & \u2248\\frac{s(6+2)-s(6)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(8)-s(6)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=6$ Andrey's speed is approximately $2.5\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
